WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.279
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade nine English.

2
00:00:06.579 --> 00:00:10.232
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.532 --> 00:00:18.653
Unit nineteen: Writing: Paragraphs, Letters and Emails. Today you will write a clear paragraph and a short letter or email.

4
00:00:18.953 --> 00:00:21.571
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:22.533 --> 00:00:25.952
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:26.817 --> 00:00:27.841
Paragraph.

7
00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:31.894
Paragraph means a group of sentences about one idea.

8
00:00:32.483 --> 00:00:33.821
Write a paragraph.

9
00:00:34.417 --> 00:00:36.906
Your turn. Say: Paragraph.

10
00:00:39.767 --> 00:00:40.768
Paragraph.

11
00:00:41.517 --> 00:00:42.866
Topic sentence.

12
00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:46.906
Topic sentence means the sentence with the main idea.

13
00:00:47.517 --> 00:00:49.412
Begin with a topic sentence.

14
00:00:50.017 --> 00:00:53.087
Your turn. Say: Topic sentence.

15
00:00:55.933 --> 00:00:57.341
Topic sentence.

16
00:00:58.083 --> 00:00:59.630
Supporting sentence.

17
00:01:00.617 --> 00:01:03.661
Supporting sentence means a sentence that gives details.

18
00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:05.959
Add supporting sentences.

19
00:01:06.550 --> 00:01:09.887
Your turn. Say: Supporting sentence.

20
00:01:12.733 --> 00:01:14.129
Supporting sentence.

21
00:01:14.883 --> 00:01:15.896
Conclusion.

22
00:01:16.883 --> 00:01:19.092
Conclusion means the final sentence.

23
00:01:19.683 --> 00:01:21.172
End with a conclusion.

24
00:01:21.783 --> 00:01:24.668
Your turn. Say: Conclusion.

25
00:01:27.533 --> 00:01:28.558
Conclusion.

26
00:01:29.317 --> 00:01:30.236
Greeting.

27
00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:33.308
Greeting means the opening of a letter.

28
00:01:33.917 --> 00:01:35.417
Dear Sir is a greeting.

29
00:01:36.017 --> 00:01:38.657
Your turn. Say: Greeting.

30
00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:42.315
Greeting.

31
00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:43.900
Closing.

32
00:01:44.917 --> 00:01:46.858
Closing means the polite ending.

33
00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:49.531
Yours sincerely is a closing.

34
00:01:50.117 --> 00:01:52.061
Your turn. Say: Closing.

35
00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:55.692
Closing.

36
00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:57.625
Linking word.

37
00:01:58.617 --> 00:02:01.696
Linking word means a word that connects ideas.

38
00:02:02.283 --> 00:02:03.900
First, then and finally.

39
00:02:04.483 --> 00:02:07.287
Your turn. Say: Linking word.

40
00:02:10.133 --> 00:02:11.274
Linking word.

41
00:02:12.017 --> 00:02:12.890
Proofread.

42
00:02:13.883 --> 00:02:16.475
Proofread means to check writing for mistakes.

43
00:02:17.083 --> 00:02:18.282
Proofread your work.

44
00:02:18.883 --> 00:02:21.710
Your turn. Say: Proofread.

45
00:02:24.567 --> 00:02:25.626
Proofread.

46
00:02:26.433 --> 00:02:30.235
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:31.083 --> 00:02:33.617
Visal, how do I write a good paragraph?

48
00:02:34.717 --> 00:02:45.705
Begin with a topic sentence that gives the main idea. Then write two or three supporting sentences with reasons or examples, and end with a short concluding sentence.

49
00:02:46.817 --> 00:02:48.793
How do I write a letter or an email?

50
00:02:49.883 --> 00:03:00.059
Start with a greeting such as Dear Ms. Lee or Hi Anna. Give the reason for writing, answer every point, and finish with a closing and your name.

51
00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:02.790
What should I check at the end?

52
00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:11.888
Proofread for spelling, capital letters and punctuation. Check the verb tenses and make sure each sentence is clear.

53
00:03:13.033 --> 00:03:14.499
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:19.590
Grammar focus: Strategy: topic sentence, details, conclusion.

55
00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:21.112
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:21.817 --> 00:03:25.999
My favourite season is the rainy season because the countryside becomes green.

57
00:03:26.883 --> 00:03:29.997
Dear Anna, Thank you for your invitation to the party.

58
00:03:30.933 --> 00:03:40.145
Start with a topic sentence, add supporting sentences and end with a conclusion. In letters and emails, answer every point and use a polite closing.

59
00:03:40.883 --> 00:03:44.488
Be careful! Don't say: I start a letter without a greeting.

60
00:03:46.433 --> 00:03:48.236
Say: I start with a greeting.

61
00:03:48.536 --> 00:03:49.769
Begin politely.

62
00:03:50.567 --> 00:03:53.103
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.110
A Short Email.

64
00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:58.002
Vanna writes an email to her friend Anna.

65
00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:02.184
She begins with Dear Anna and thanks her for the invitation.

66
00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:05.861
She says she can come on Saturday at four o'clock.

67
00:04:06.867 --> 00:04:08.994
She asks Anna what she should bring.

68
00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:12.023
She ends with Best wishes and her name.

69
00:04:13.133 --> 00:04:17.100
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:20.066
A paragraph begins with a blank.

71
00:04:20.366 --> 00:04:24.205
A, number. B, topic sentence. C, closing.

72
00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:30.184
The answer is B: topic sentence.

73
00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:33.117
An email begins with a blank.

74
00:04:33.417 --> 00:04:37.036
A, signature. B, date only. C, greeting.

75
00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:42.356
The answer is C: greeting.

76
00:04:43.517 --> 00:04:45.342
What does Vanna thank Anna for?

77
00:04:45.642 --> 00:04:49.470
A, the invitation. B, the gift. C, the book.

78
00:04:53.033 --> 00:04:55.486
The answer is A: the invitation.

79
00:04:56.650 --> 00:04:57.953
At the end you should blank.

80
00:04:58.253 --> 00:05:01.860
A, erase. B, proofread. C, stop.

81
00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:07.585
The answer is B: proofread.

82
00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:10.262
What time can Vanna come?

83
00:05:10.562 --> 00:05:14.401
A, nine o'clock. B, noon. C, four o'clock.

84
00:05:17.967 --> 00:05:19.966
The answer is C: four o'clock.

85
00:05:21.167 --> 00:05:24.109
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:24.950 --> 00:05:27.472
Write two sentences about your favourite season.

87
00:05:36.283 --> 00:05:37.668
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:37.968 --> 00:05:51.406
My favourite season is the rainy season because the countryside becomes green and the air is fresh. I also like it because my family cooks warm soup and we talk together at home.

89
00:05:51.706 --> 00:05:53.287
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:54.183 --> 00:05:59.959
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: topic sentence, details, conclusion.

91
00:06:00.259 --> 00:06:04.397
Today's value is communication. Speak clearly and listen carefully.

92
00:06:04.697 --> 00:06:07.373
See you in Unit twenty. Goodbye!

93
00:06:07.673 --> 00:06:10.302
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

